course: dictionary
lesson: 12824
title: Emission: what gets sent out
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An emission is something sent out into the air, such as gas, heat or light. The verb is emit, which means to send out. Context gives the clues: «The bus left a cloud of black emissions as it pulled away.» Black smoke coming out of a bus is something being sent out, so emissions means things sent out into the air.
explain: In science and environment lessons, emissions usually means harmful gases, such as carbon dioxide from cars, factories and power stations. «Cutting emissions helps slow climate change.» The words cutting and climate change are your clues: people want less of these gases, so emissions must be the gases themselves.
explain: The word has a second meaning: the act of sending something out. «The emission of light from a star can travel for millions of years.» Here emission is the sending out of the light, not the light itself. Check the meaning by swapping it into the sentence: «The sending out of light from a star» still makes sense.
fact: An emission is something sent out into the air, such as gas, heat or light.
fact: «Emissions» often means harmful gases from cars, factories and power stations.
fact: «Carbon emissions» are gases that contain carbon, such as carbon dioxide.
fact: «Zero emissions» means sending out no harmful gases, as some electric cars do.
fact: «Cut emissions» means send out less, so the air is cleaner.
exercise: «The bus left a cloud of black emissions as it pulled away.» What are the emissions here? | Seats for passengers | *Gases sent out into the air | Loud music from the radio
exercise: Which phrase means a vehicle that sends out no harmful gases? | Zero gravity | *Zero emissions | Zero hour
exercise: «Factories must cut emissions to protect the air.» What does «cut emissions» mean? | Make the factory bigger | Paint the factory walls | *Send out fewer harmful gases
test: «The factory's carbon emissions rose again last year.» What does emissions mean here? | *Harmful gases sent out into the air | Workers who go home early | Music played in the factory
test: «The telescope recorded the emission of light from a distant star.» What does emission mean here? | A map of the stars | A light that is switched off | *The act of sending light out
exam: «Reducing emissions helps slow climate change, so cities are building bike lanes.» What does reducing emissions mean? | Planting more trees | *Sending out fewer harmful gases | Building taller buildings | Making more noise
